From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] map-controller: send the Controller Capability TLV at two octets

MediaTek's EasyMesh R3 mapd accepts the Controller Capability TLV (0xDD)
only at a length of exactly 2. At length 1, which is what we sent, or
with the TLV absent, it discards the whole AP-Autoconfiguration Response,
does not record the sender as the controller and never sends WSC M1:

  parse_controller_cap_tlv: error CONTROLLER_CAPABILITY_LEN length is 1 incorrect
  topo_srv_get_controller_device: controller not found in MAP dev list

Over a wired link it got configured anyway; over Wi-Fi it searched for
112 s, gave up, dropped its backhaul and started again, so a MediaTek
agent never took our SSIDs and kept its factory ones (found on hardware
2026-09-18; the length check was read from its mapd disassembly: len == 2,
flags in the first octet, bit 6 used).

The TLV now carries the flags octet and one reserved zero octet. Our own
readers are unaffected: the ieee1905 validator refuses only fewer than
one octet, and map-agent reads the first one.

Signed-off-by: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/src/cntlr_tlv.c b/src/cntlr_tlv.c
index 645b8ca..d2b7f4e 100644
--- a/src/cntlr_tlv.c
+++ b/src/cntlr_tlv.c
@@ -2453,7 +2453,23 @@ int cntlr_gen_cntlr_capability(struct controller *c, struct cmdu_buff *frm, uint
 
 	data->flag = caps;
 
-	t->len = sizeof(*data);
+	/* Two octets, the second one zero.
+	 *
+	 * The TLV carries one octet of flags, and one octet is what we sent.
+	 * MediaTek's mapd (EasyMesh R3, reference box 2026-09-18) accepts this
+	 * TLV only at a length of exactly 2 and reads the flags from the first
+	 * octet; at any other length, or with the TLV missing, it drops the
+	 * whole AP-Autoconfiguration Response ("CONTROLLER_CAPABILITY_LEN
+	 * length is 1 incorrect"), never records us as the controller and never
+	 * sends M1. Over Wi-Fi that left it retrying for 112 s and then
+	 * dropping its backhaul, in a loop.
+	 *
+	 * A trailing reserved octet costs a reader of the flags nothing: our
+	 * own validator only refuses fewer than one octet and map-agent reads
+	 * the first one.
+	 */
+	data->rsvd[0] = 0;
+	t->len = sizeof(*data) + 1;
 	if (cmdu_put_tlv(frm, t))
 		return -1;
 
